447	 *
448	 * Description:
449	 *   This method will send a block of data on the UART.
450	 *
451	 *   The USB-Serial-JTAG TX FIFO is a 64-byte hardware FIFO.  The per-byte
452	 *   esp_send() path issues a wr_done flush for every character; if a flush
453	 *   lands while the USB engine is still transmitting the previous packet it
454	 *   can be dropped, leaving bytes stuck in the FIFO with SERIAL_IN_EP_DATA_
455	 *   FREE latched low and IN_EMPTY never re-asserting -- the console wedges
456	 *   at an arbitrary byte count.  Writing a chunk and flushing ONCE (the
457	 *   ESP-IDF driver pattern) avoids racing the engine, so this method is used
458	 *   for the interrupt-driven drain while esp_send() remains for the polled
459	 *   paths (esp_usbserial_write / dbg_putc).
