729	   * services UART0: its interrupt line stays asserted (floating RX / stale
730	   * FIFO), and the first driver that shares cpuint 5 through esp_intr_alloc
731	   * (the JPEG encoder) and enables CLIC 21 turns that asserted line into an
732	   * unstoppable level storm - shared_intr_isr only knows the JPEG vector, the
733	   * JPEG status register reads 0 (no encode), nothing is cleared, and the
734	   * dispatch re-fires forever ('k' flood).  This was the root cause of the
735	   * jpegenc hang.
736	   *
737	   * Disable UART0's peripheral interrupt and re-route its source to the
738	   * reserved INT_MUX_DISABLED_INTNO (CPU int 6, never enabled) so UART0 can
